# Excel export rules

The output is not "an Excel file". It is a reproduction of a specific paper form that
someone prints and signs. Layout fidelity is the requirement.

## Library

ExcelJS, exact version pinned in `package.json`. Do not float it, do not swap to
SheetJS (its community edition has limited styling support), and do not add
`xlsx-js-style`.

Generation happens **synchronously inside the request handler** and streams back. No
background job, no queue, no file storage. At 40 sheets of 25 rows this is well under
a second.

## Workbook structure

One file per generation:

- **Sheet 1, `REKAP`** — one row per technician: trip count, BBM total, Toll dan Parkir
  total, Makan total, grand total, and a year to date column. Branch subtotal rows at
  the bottom.
- **Sheets 2..N** — one per technician, named after the technician.

## Technician sheet layout, exact

Title block, then these columns in this order:

`TANGGAL`, `TUJUAN`, `KOTA`, `KM AWAL`, `KM AKHIR`, `JARAK`, `BBM`,
`TOLL DAN PARKIR`, `MAKAN`, `KETERANGAN`

Then a `Sub Total` row, a `Grand Total` row, and the `Pemeriksa` and `Staf HRD GA`
signature block.

**`TOLL DAN PARKIR` is `tollAmount + parkingAmount` summed at render time.** The
database stores them as two separate columns and that does not change. Summing for
display is fine; merging them in storage is not.

## Print setup, per sheet, required

Every technician sheet sets all of these. Missing any one is a defect, not a polish item:

```ts
worksheet.pageSetup = {
  orientation: 'landscape',
  paperSize: 9,                    // A4
  fitToPage: true,
  fitToWidth: 1,
  fitToHeight: 0,                  // 1 page wide, unlimited tall
  margins: { left: 0.5, right: 0.5, top: 0.5, bottom: 0.5, header: 0.3, footer: 0.3 },
  printArea: 'A1:J40',             // set explicitly, never left open
}
worksheet.pageSetup.printTitlesRow = '1:2'   // header row repeats on every page
worksheet.headerFooter = { oddFooter: '&LDicetak &D &T&RHalaman &P dari &N' }
```

**Set `printArea` explicitly.** Left open, empty columns to the right spill onto a
second page, and the whole point of the layout is lost.

## Number formatting

Currency cells use an Indonesian thousand separator with no decimals:
`'#,##0'` with the workbook locale, rendering as `1.110.500`.

Values written to cells are the stored integers. Never recompute a total in the export
layer. If the sheet total does not match the application total, the bug is upstream and
must be fixed there.

## Scope

`GET /api/exports/monthly` must enforce branch scope in the query like every other
route. A branch head may only pass their own `branchId`. Omitting `branchId` returns
all branches for `hr` only, never for a branch head.

This endpoint is the easiest one to forget and the worst to get wrong: it hands over an
entire branch in a single file.

## File name

`Biaya-Operasional-Teknisi-{YYYY}-{MM}-{BRANCHCODE}.xlsx`

## Verification when changing anything here

Print a 22 trip technician sheet to PDF. It must be exactly one page. Print a 60 trip
sheet: every page after the first must repeat the column header row.
